Revision history for Cavil::CLI

0.01   2026-08-28
        - First release: a command-line client for Cavil that checks whether the code in a git change set or a
          directory already exists in what Cavil has indexed (open source and commercial), reporting its
          license and risk for a developer's laptop or CI.
        - "check" checks the current git change set by default, or a whole tree given a path or --all; a risk
          gate (--fail-on-risk, default 5) sets the exit code, with json output for CI.
        - "whoami" verifies the configured URL and token, and "config" saves them to ~/.config/cavil-cli
          (the token read from a hidden prompt, never the command line).
        - Recognizes files by content hash first and only searches the residual, with an aggressive
          per-instance cache so repeated and interrupted scans put almost no load on the server.
        - Filters out noise: a repository's own license files, self-matches against its own indexed package
          (--exclude-package), and excluded paths such as test fixtures (--exclude-path).
